("grow.room.jesus", "isa", "ReadingSection")
("grow.room.jesus", "anchor", "jesus-grew")
("grow.room.jesus", "title", "Jesus had growing to do")
("grow.room.jesus", "paragraph", "Luke tells a story about Jesus at twelve. After a visit to Jerusalem, Mary and Joseph discover he is missing from their travelling group. They return and find him in the temple, among the teachers, listening, asking questions and giving answers that astonish the people who hear him.")
("grow.room.jesus", "paragraph", "There is worry in the story, too. His parents have been searching anxiously. Jesus speaks about his Father, and they do not understand what he means. He goes home with them to Nazareth. Luke closes by saying that Jesus continued to grow in wisdom and stature, and in favour with God and people.")
("grow.room.jesus", "paragraph", "Christians believe Jesus is the Son of God. In Luke’s account, his human life includes learning, relationships and time. We are given very little detail about his teenage years, but we are told that he grew.")
("grow.room.jesus", "paragraph", "I find that encouraging. Growing belongs within a life lived close to God. You can be loved now and still have things to learn.")

("grow.room.scripture", "isa", "ScriptureReading")
("grow.room.scripture", "label", "Read the encounter in Luke")
("grow.room.scripture", "reference", "Luke 2:41–52")
("grow.room.scripture", "href", "https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Luke%202%3A41-52&version=WEB")
("grow.room.scripture", "note", "Watch for the listening, the questions, the worried parents and the return home. What catches your attention?")

("grow.room.questions", "isa", "ReadingSection")
("grow.room.questions", "anchor", "your-questions")
("grow.room.questions", "title", "You can take your questions seriously")
("grow.room.questions", "paragraph", "Notice Jesus listening and asking questions. His understanding is remarkable, yet there is a conversation happening. Attention and questions belong in it.")
("grow.room.questions", "paragraph", "You might have questions about a Bible passage, something said at church, or whether a belief you have inherited makes sense to you. You might wonder why people who speak about love can be unkind. Some questions arrive because you are curious. Others arrive because something hurts.")
("grow.room.questions", "paragraph", "You can give those questions words. You do not need to turn them into a confident speech before bringing them to someone you trust.")
("grow.room.questions", "saying", "I don’t understand this part.")
("grow.room.questions", "saying", "Why do we believe that?")
("grow.room.questions", "saying", "Can I tell you what troubles me about it?")
("grow.room.questions", "after", "A good conversation gives both people something to do. You can explain what you mean, hear an answer, think about it and ask again. The person answering may need to look something up or reconsider their own explanation. Adults have learning to do as well.")
("grow.room.questions", "after", "Some questions take a long time. You can keep reading, praying and talking while an answer is still taking shape.")

("grow.room.pause", "isa", "ReadingPause")
("grow.room.pause", "afterSection", "grow.room.questions")
("grow.room.pause", "label", "A little room to pause")
("grow.room.pause", "text", "You can be loved now and still have things to learn.")
("grow.room.pause", "note", "Stay with that for a moment, if you like.")

("grow.room.interests", "isa", "ReadingSection")
("grow.room.interests", "anchor", "changing-interests")
("grow.room.interests", "title", "Your interests have room to change")
("grow.room.interests", "paragraph", "Perhaps you love drawing now and later discover that you enjoy building things. Perhaps a subject you found dull suddenly becomes interesting because someone explains it differently. Perhaps you try something you expected to love and discover you would rather do something else.")
("grow.room.interests", "paragraph", "You have learned something in each case.")
("grow.room.interests", "paragraph", "There is value in staying with a difficult skill long enough to improve. There is also value in finding out that a particular activity is not for you. Working out the difference can take practice, conversation and a little patience.")
("grow.room.interests", "paragraph", "You are allowed to enjoy things before you know whether they will become a qualification, a job or a lifelong interest. Make the thing. Learn the song. Read the strange book. See where the question leads.")
("grow.room.interests", "paragraph", "Following Jesus can shape how you explore: with honesty, care for other people and a willingness to learn. There is plenty to practise within an ordinary day, even when your future remains uncertain.")

("grow.room.steps", "isa", "ReadingSection")
("grow.room.steps", "anchor", "one-small-step")
("grow.room.steps", "title", "There is a next step you can take")
("grow.room.steps", "paragraph", "Having room to grow includes taking responsibility for what you can do today.")
("grow.room.steps", "paragraph", "If you interrupt someone, you can stop and let them finish. If a task is confusing, you can ask for help. If you discover you were wrong, you can change your answer. If you hurt someone, you can name what you did and begin to put it right.")
("grow.room.steps", "paragraph", "You may still feel awkward afterwards. The other person may need time. Learning a better way can involve trying again tomorrow.")
("grow.room.steps", "paragraph", "Much of growing happens through small choices like these. Other people may hardly notice them. You might notice that a conversation went a little better, or that you asked for help sooner, or that you managed to listen when you wanted the last word.")
("grow.room.steps", "paragraph", "Growth also has different paces. You may need more time, clearer instructions, a quieter place or another way to express yourself. It is reasonable to ask for what helps you participate.")
("grow.room.steps", "paragraph", "And there should be time to enjoy your life: friends, games, making things, being outdoors, laughing at something ridiculous. You do not have to turn every enjoyable moment into a lesson about improving yourself.")

("grow.room.interrupted", "isa", "PracticeExample")
("grow.room.interrupted", "situation", "You interrupted")
("grow.room.interrupted", "response", "Sorry. You were still speaking. Go on.")
("grow.room.confused", "isa", "PracticeExample")
("grow.room.confused", "situation", "You need help")
("grow.room.confused", "response", "Could you show me that another way?")
("grow.room.wrong", "isa", "PracticeExample")
("grow.room.wrong", "situation", "You changed your mind")
("grow.room.wrong", "response", "I hadn’t thought of that. I see it differently now.")

("grow.room.begin", "isa", "ReadingSection")
("grow.room.begin", "anchor", "begin-here")
("grow.room.begin", "title", "You can begin here")
("grow.room.begin", "paragraph", "Perhaps the future still feels enormous. Perhaps you are excited about it. Perhaps it depends on the day.")
("grow.room.begin", "paragraph", "You can bring the person you are today into prayer: curious, tired, hopeful, unsure, or some mixture you cannot easily name. You do not have to tidy all of that into impressive words.")
("grow.room.begin", "paragraph", "Luke’s glimpse of Jesus growing invites us to take the years of learning seriously. There is a life to live while you are becoming: people to listen to, things to discover, choices to make, help to receive and good things to enjoy.")

("grow.room.question", "isa", "ReflectionQuestion")
("grow.room.question", "label", "A question to carry")
("grow.room.question", "text", "Where do you feel under pressure to have everything worked out already?")
("grow.room.question", "note", "You could think about it privately, write a few words or talk with someone you trust. You can take your time.")
("grow.room.practice", "isa", "ReadingPractice")
("grow.room.practice", "label", "Something to try this week")
("grow.room.practice", "text", "Choose one small thing you would like to understand or learn. Ask a question, give it a little time, or ask someone to show you how.")
("grow.room.practice", "followup", "At the end of the week, notice what you discovered and what you might try next.")
